:-0.7338425517082214,"token":"."}],"message":{"content":"Echo State Networks (ESNs) are a type of recurrent neural network used for processing time-series data. They consist of a large, fixed-size hidden layer called the reservoir, which is typically sparsely connected and has no weights that are adjusted during training. The weights are usually set randomly. Training involves only adjusting the readout weights that map the reservoir's state to the output. Reservoirs are trained by simply running input data through the network and adjusting the output weights to minimize error.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1060,"prompt_eval_duration":45589000,"total_duration":1303127800}}